  "notes": "{投薬|とうやく} refers to the administration of medicine by a healthcare professional. The kanji combine {投|とう} (to throw/deliver) and {薬|やく} (medicine). It is a formal, medical term.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {投薬|とうやく}する: to administer medicine\n- {投薬|とうやく}を{受|う}ける: to receive medication\n- {投薬|とうやく}{治療|ちりょう}: drug therapy\n- {投薬|とうやく}を{中止|ちゅうし}する: to discontinue medication\n- {投薬|とうやく}{量|りょう}: dosage\n\nRELATED MEDICAL TERMS:\n- {処方|しょほう}: prescription (what the doctor writes)\n- {服薬|ふくやく}: taking medicine (from the patient's perspective)\n- {調剤|ちょうざい}: dispensing medicine (pharmacist's work)\n- {点滴|てんてき}: IV drip\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is a formal medical term used by healthcare professionals. In everyday conversation, {薬|くすり}を{飲|の}む (to take medicine) or {薬|くすり}をもらう (to receive medicine) is more natural.",
